  "title": "Must See Monday – Events of the Week: Manuelita, The Lone Bellow &#038; Independent Venue Week: Bad Sounds",
  "content": "<p><em>25th January 2016</em></p>\n<p><strong>TIP OF THE WEEK<br /></strong><strong>What</strong>: <span>Manuelita</span> // <strong>Where</strong>: The Wardrobe Theatre // <strong>When</strong>: Thu 28th &#8211; Sat 30th Jan (8pm) // <strong>Cost: </strong>£8</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://thewardrobetheatre.com/livetheatre/manuelita/\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Main-Image2-724x1024.jpg\" alt=\"Main-Image2-724x1024\" width=\"724\" height=\"1024\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-10942\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Main-Image2-724x1024.jpg 724w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Main-Image2-724x1024-212x300.jpg 212w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Main-Image2-724x1024-318x450.jpg 318w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 724px) 100vw, 724px\" /></a></p>\n<p>Revolutionary, proto-feminist, underground spy and the beating heart of South American liberation, Manuela Saenz died in poverty, all but forgotten by the history books – until now.</p>\n<p>Blending storytelling, physical theatre, comedy and live music, Lecoq-trained Tamsin Clarke brings Manuelaʼs story of love, loss and revolution vibrantly to life. With accompaniment by Colombian musician and guitarist Camilo Menjura (UK Latin American Musician Of The Year 2014), Manuelita promises audiences a heart-swelling, toe-tapping night out at the theatre.</p>\n<p><strong style=\"line-height: 1.5;\">To find out more click <a href=\"http://thewardrobetheatre.com/livetheatre/manuelita/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</strong></p>\n<p><iframe loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://player.vimeo.com/video/113487050?dnt=1&amp;app_id=122963\" width=\"640\" height=\"360\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\"></iframe></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>OTHER TIPS<br /></strong></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>The Lone Bellow @ Thekla // Weds 27th Jan // Cost: £13.20<br /><a href=\"http://www.theklabristol.co.uk/live/572/the-lone-bellow\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/1035x690-20131213-lonebellows-04-x1800-1386960730.jpg\" alt=\"1035x690-20131213-lonebellows-04-x1800-1386960730\" width=\"1035\" height=\"690\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-10943\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/1035x690-20131213-lonebellows-04-x1800-1386960730.jpg 1035w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/1035x690-20131213-lonebellows-04-x1800-1386960730-300x200.jpg 300w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/1035x690-20131213-lonebellows-04-x1800-1386960730-768x512.jpg 768w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/1035x690-20131213-lonebellows-04-x1800-1386960730-675x450.jpg 675w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/1035x690-20131213-lonebellows-04-x1800-1386960730-120x80.jpg 120w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1035px) 100vw, 1035px\" /></a></strong><span>This alt-country Brooklyn trio, comprising Zach Williams, Kanene Donehey Pipkin and Brian Elmquist, write melancholic lyrics on relationships, love, grief, and spirituality with swelling three-part harmonies and rousing group-sung choruses. Their smooth country-folk sound has seen them compared to The Lumineers and The Civil Wars.</span></p>\n<p><strong style=\"line-height: 1.5;\">To find out more then click <a href=\"http://www.theklabristol.co.uk/live/572/the-lone-bellow\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</strong></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Independent Venue Week: Bad Sounds @ The Louisiana <strong style=\"line-height: 1.5;\">// Sat 30th Jan // Cost: £9<br /><a href=\"http://www.thelouisiana.net/events/30-jan-16-independent-venue-week-the-louisiana/\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Z3dqIMIf.jpg\" alt=\"Z3dqIMIf\" width=\"512\" height=\"512\" class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-10944\" srcset=\"https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Z3dqIMIf.jpg 512w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Z3dqIMIf-150x150.jpg 150w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Z3dqIMIf-300x300.jpg 300w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Z3dqIMIf-450x450.jpg 450w, https://www.thefixmagazine.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/01/Z3dqIMIf-45x45.jpg 45w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 512px) 100vw, 512px\" /></a></strong></strong></p>\n<p>Last January The Louisiana put on one of their favourite events so far, over three floors of the venue, to celebrate Independent Venue Week. </p>\n<p>They are excited to announce that they are doing it all again to kick off 2016.</p>\n<p>Upstairs will be more lively and the cellar more intimate, with some interesting things on the ground floor too.<strong><strong style=\"line-height: 1.5;\"><br /></strong><br /></strong><em></em><strong>To find out more click <a href=\"http://www.thelouisiana.net/events/30-jan-16-independent-venue-week-the-louisiana/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</strong></p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Kevin McGough</strong></p>\n<p></p>",
